   "html_text": "Two final remarks about Kilwardby’s life and thought. First, although he came to be known as a polemicist, the leitmotif of his work was to harmonize a certain understanding of Aristotle with a certain understanding of Augustine. Second, his life’s work seems to move against the mainstream of the century he lived in. Most authors had adopted the new Aristotelian philosophy that new translations of known works and especially recently discovered ones (to the Latin West, that is) just made availabl",
   "md_text": "Two final remarks about Kilwardby’s life and thought. First, although he came to be known as a polemicist, the leitmotif of his work was to harmonize a certain understanding of Aristotle with a certain understanding of Augustine. Second, his life’s work seems to move against the mainstream of the century he lived in. Most authors had adopted the new Aristotelian philosophy that new translations of known works and especially recently discovered ones (to the Latin West, that is) just made availabl"
  }
